################################################################################
# Trpiboot DRaspberry Pi 5 specifics

	This loader is started directly by the Raspberry Pi 5 VPU firmware,
	with no EFI and no EDK2 in the boot path.  The device tree comes from
	the firmware as a physical address in x0; there is no EFI memory map,
	so all memory information comes from the tree's /memory node.

	The console is the SoC PL011 at 0x107d001000, which the firmware has
	already configured to 115200 8N1 before entry.

	md0: is the image the firmware loaded with the config.txt line

		initramfs <file> 0x30000000

	so it is available with no storage driver at all.  The image must
	start at or above the end of the staging window (0x30000000).

################################################################################
# Trpiboot_initrd_root DUse the initrd as the kernel's root

	set rpiboot_initrd_root=YES

	Copies md0: behind the kernel as an mfs_root module at boot, so the
	kernel's md(4) attaches it as md0 and can mount it as root with
	vfs.root.mountfrom="ufs:/dev/md0".  Used by the live and installer
	image.  Left unset, the initrd only supplies the kernel and its
	modules and root is found elsewhere, as on an installed system.

################################################################################
